export const body = "<p><strong>General Information</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Technical Artist :</strong></p>\n\n<ul><li>Bui Trung Dung</li></ul>\n\n\n<p><strong>Work type</strong>: Champion's Skin production ( end to end )</p>\n\n<p><strong>Tasks</strong>: Deliver a full skin production ( Model, Animation, VFX )</p>\n\n\n<h2>Introduction</h2>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span>The project, also known as the project, is the project that isn't a really hard project from both art and technical side. It's really basic and understandable knowledge (and sometime sound really simple). But, a 10 years old game here is not an simple task that could easily meet the quality in art style, as well as working directly with an in-house game engine from client.</p>\n\n<p>In this article, it will be mainly share about role and responsibility of the a Pipeline Technical Artist in the game project, let's have some Introduction about the project first.</p>\n\n<h3>About me</h3>\n\n<p>My name is Bui Trung Dung, and I'm working as Pipeline Technical Artist in the game, I've been working more than a year in this project.</p>\n\n<p><strong>What is Champion Skin ?</strong></p>\n\n<p>A Champion Skin is an alternate appearance (skin) for the base character in the game ( champion ). This make the player having a different \"flavor\" when playing the same champion again and again with thought feeling bored. However, each skin have it's own story behind it (also know as thematic ) and it's not really related to the base champion's story.</p>\n\n<p>When working on the project, it's important to understand the thematic and the champion, this can help the team understand the art quality that the team is needed for the product that they are working on</p>\n\n\n<p><em>RPG skins</em></p>\n\n\n<p><em>Lux base Champion</em></p>\n\n\n<p>Dark Cosmic Lux Skin</p>\n\n<p><strong>How are we working on the project ?</strong></p>\n\n<ul><li><strong>Core Software:</strong></li></ul>\n\n<ul><li><strong>Game Engine: </strong>A game engine that's developed in house by the client, this is the main goal of the project because eventually everything have to be published in-game for the results. This is also the main working environment for VFX artist to working on.</li><li><strong>Maya</strong> (specific version) : This is the main working platform for artists when working on the project. There are also a custom tools and plug-in that's been deployed by client to make sure the team following the same work-flow as their end. The tools in maya also help to convert meshes, rig, animation file into game engine.</li><li><strong>Photoshop:</strong> This is the main working platform for texture in-game, any texture work ( Model texture, VFX texture ) have to be exported from here into game engine.</li><li><strong>Perforce (P4V)</strong> : This is the main version control application for the team to work in across discipline as sending their work over. The server we are using was from clients, there for all our work are sending directly to client eventually.</li></ul>\n\n<ul><li><strong>External Communication platform</strong></li></ul>\n\n<ul><li><strong>Slack</strong> : Most<strong> </strong>communication, discussion (both art and technical) with client are going through here</li><li><strong>Artella: </strong>This is the platform for art review ( record in-game in video/ sending image ), Most of art feedback from client are going through here</li><li><strong>Jira:</strong> This is the platform for champion skin technical issue. When all art feedback are being approved, it doesn't mean it has no technical at all. After the production are approved, a QA test will be started and sent back any ticket issue that they found out.</li></ul>\n\n<p><strong>What are </strong><strong>TA's tasks on the project</strong> <strong>?</strong></p>\n\n<ul><li>Finding potential technical issues on the production</li><li>P4V version control.</li><li>Tools, game engine, Art troubleshooting.</li><li>Play as a cohesive role between team and client to resolve art production.</li><li>Managing Jira ticket</li><li>Enhance team with technical knowledge.</li></ul>\n\n<p>In short, is to unblock artists from any technical issue and also to communicate with team member what is the best approach for the production that can reach the goal in art, but still meet the technical requirement.</p>\n\n<h3>Responsibility</h3>\n\n<h4><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span>Finding potential technical issues on the production</h4>\n\n<p>It's always better to be prepare for the potential issue before it's actually happening. This will help the team to work on the product smoothly without running into any issues that's already heads-up . Because sometime the issue can cause the team to re-do everything all over again, so knowing them first before it happened can help the team meet the deadline without any redundant work that can cause the production later on.</p>\n\n<p>In the game, there are some task the TA will be working on in a production line, they are:</p>\n\n<ul><li>Concept and idea sweep</li><li>Animation sweep</li><li>Play game</li></ul>\n\n<p>So in the production timelines , we can arrange the task follow like this.</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Pre-production</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Milestone 1 - 2</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Milestone 3 - 4</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Concept and idea sweep</p>\n<p>Play game</p></td><td><p>Animation sweep ( after proxy model )</p></td><td><p>Play game ( when the skin is final )</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n<p><strong><br></strong><strong>Pre-production</strong></p>\n\n<p>Before the production start, understanding the brief is important, therefore it's also a good time to heads-up for the time first</p>\n\n<p>In the game, by playing the game with the champion that we are going to make a new skin will help us understand how the character play out in game and is there any unique situation that we haven't encountered before. Also, sometime it could help the team know if there is any additional scopes that is needed.</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Taliyah</strong></p><p>Taliyah is one of the champion that has a lot of meshes in her VFX as well as her interaction in-game.</p>\n<p>Usually VFX team only work on Texture and how to emit the particles, so this will be an addition scope for Model as some other discipline as well. So spot them out earlier can help the team have a better estimate as they are additional workload that team are needed to work on.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0bbac87919a06bce9c36.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0bbac87919a06bce9c36.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"483\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>VFX meshes shown on her Q skill, The mesh will need an additional concept for this</em></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/74e06814f785db426c47.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/74e06814f785db426c47.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"435\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 7\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>VFX meshes shown on her W skill, the VFX need new concept, model as well as animation, rigging for the mesh</em></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/86522ed72edb590edfbc.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/86522ed72edb590edfbc.webp\" width=\"1041\" height=\"697\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 8\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>VFX meshes shown on her E skill, the mesh need a few different variant and generate randomly</em></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/dff83cfc6d2575ebb62b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/dff83cfc6d2575ebb62b.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"663\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 9\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>VFX mesh on her Ultimate skill, this require a new concept for it as well</em></p>\n<p><em><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7d2b16e9a0fb5888492f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7d2b16e9a0fb5888492f.webp\" width=\"943\" height=\"764\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 10\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></em></p>\n<p><em>Rock mesh appear when she stay near the rock wall</em></p>\n<p><em><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/55023ff5858167428559.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/55023ff5858167428559.webp\" width=\"561\" height=\"554\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 11\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></em><em><br></em></p>\n<p><em>Other rock mesh on one of her emote in-game</em></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Gnar</strong></p><p>Gnar is one of the case that the champion that is changed to a different from when he reached maximum in his rage bar</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/8834b0c4b1bfbd39350c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/8834b0c4b1bfbd39350c.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 12\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>Gnar on his normal stage</em></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5e147de821b501a0eaca.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5e147de821b501a0eaca.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 13\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>Gnar when the rage bar is full, his texture changed</em></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b935023f36cfb9f4dee4.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b935023f36cfb9f4dee4.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 14\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><em>Mega Gnar form</em></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/8eeafe949308c4250124.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/8eeafe949308c4250124.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 15\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>Addition mesh for his Gnar's animation</em></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/11d65f2a40fff55aae11.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/11d65f2a40fff55aae11.webp\" width=\"550\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:550px\" alt=\"Illustration 16\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>Addition mesh for Mega Gnar's VFX</em></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Kayle</strong></p><p>Kayle is one of the really special case in the game, the appearance changed every time she leveling up. There for this is really critical to look for the differences and break down the scope and what need to be done in this champion</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c19103bb6775eb1096af.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c19103bb6775eb1096af.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 17\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>Kayle lv1</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/8c36a3aea99506786574.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/8c36a3aea99506786574.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 18\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>Kayle lv6</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e61b94a743f8ff94c4a3.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e61b94a743f8ff94c4a3.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 19\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>Kayle lv11</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/cb8e3142368bba85c457.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/cb8e3142368bba85c457.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 20\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>Kayle lv16</p></div>\n\n<p><strong>Concept sweep</strong> is important as well, going through the character and check for concept to compare the different in design that may cause an issue for the character ( such as clipping, animation error because of the base animation). Idea sweep (animation/ vfx idea on new skin ), can help the team to find out what issue may occur later on in production ( such as weapon being shaky during animation )</p>\n\n<p>&lt;example on Ziggs/ Katarina )</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Taric</strong></p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/12793848e46e239e3743.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/12793848e46e239e3743.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"608\" style=\"--source-width:547px\" alt=\"Illustration 21\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>RPG Taric has a lot of difference compare to the original skin</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/2eacf7338904cfc6285c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/2eacf7338904cfc6285c.webp\" width=\"519\" height=\"511\" style=\"--source-width:406px\" alt=\"Illustration 22\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>There are a lot of items around his hips ( a scroll and a book on both side )</p>\n<p>He doesn't have a cape .</p>\n<p>This can cause a lot of issue later on on his rig, so a concept adjust is needed</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d541976476df8e991312.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d541976476df8e991312.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"689\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 23\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Katarina</strong></p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3e1c41bf93ff6c7576c5.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3e1c41bf93ff6c7576c5.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"561\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 24\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>Katarina Bloodmoon concept is pretty straight forward, as the model isn't missing or added a props that is questionable.</p>\n<p>However on her recall animation idea, The character will wear a mask that were staying on her side of the mask.Your browser does not support the HTML5 video element</p>\n<p>The recall have raise a challenging part that's there isn't any joint for a mask to make an animation, so we have to add an additional joint in. By right, we're supposed not to add any additional joint inside the base character's rig because the old animation doesn't have key value for this joint, hence it will return the value to 0 and cause animation issue.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4bf5a18476d3c8fa5622.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4bf5a18476d3c8fa5622.webp\" width=\"429\" height=\"455\" style=\"--source-width:236px\" alt=\"Illustration 25\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>But after a few work around, we found a solution for it and eventually it's worked.</p></div>\n\n<p>Usually at this stage, we don't look for solution right away ( for example changing concept ), but since we are aware of it, we can prepare the solution for later.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Milestone 1 - 2</strong><strong><br></strong></p>\n\n<p>After the proxy model is done, this is a time to look for all technical issue that will be related with the skin inside the game engine. The task help both clients and the team have visibility on the actual issues that's are happened now. At this stage, all action will be called, it could be mesh adjustment, changing concept, or adjust animation or we leave it as acceptable.</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Evelynn</strong></p><p>Sugar Rush Evelynn's Joke animation clipping issue was found during animation sweep.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/db3659f3617a4f60a155.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/db3659f3617a4f60a155.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:400px\" alt=\"Illustration 26\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5ab189b9160a7556a508.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5ab189b9160a7556a508.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:400px\" alt=\"Illustration 27\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>The clipping was caused because of her new design on tail, previously it was flat and the animation was for her base design.</p>\n<p>Issue is only happened on this animation, it's an unacceptable clipping, also the since the solution can't be fixed by mesh adjustment and client don't really want to change the design for her tail, So we have to come up with a high cost solution<strong>*</strong> is to adjust the animation for her. And here is the results</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f4879915f31667a38ed6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f4879915f31667a38ed6.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:400px\" alt=\"Illustration 28\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><strong>Note *</strong> : In the game, animation fix is a high cost solution that have to be agreed by client that this is needed to fix.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Ziggs</strong></p><p>Take a look at Ziggs Champion as an example</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/a16e69ffa78cc650b488.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/a16e69ffa78cc650b488.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 29\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>Here is his SugarRush skin concept art:</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f1ad2b79f553ec08d8b6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f1ad2b79f553ec08d8b6.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"553\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 30\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>As going through the concept, we've noticed that the concept was missed out his shoulder pad. This wasn't a big concern at the beginning. However once the proxy model is done, we found out a bigger problem later on.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/68b7609b5428a3c72c41.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/68b7609b5428a3c72c41.webp\" width=\"311\" height=\"273\" style=\"--source-width:285px\" alt=\"Illustration 31\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/a17ae04b16fdaa01dab6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/a17ae04b16fdaa01dab6.webp\" width=\"551\" height=\"599\" style=\"--source-width:230px\" alt=\"Illustration 32\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>His arm is being twisted in his base animation, however the issue wasn't spotted earlier because the shoulder was covered on the base skin and on the top down view. Eventually, we've added 2 shoulder pieces and resolved the issue</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/56c2c72a0138781e9724.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/56c2c72a0138781e9724.webp\" width=\"569\" height=\"596\" style=\"--source-width:382px\" alt=\"Illustration 33\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Renekton</strong></p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5d1364b828c601e286b7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5d1364b828c601e286b7.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 34\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>In Renekton's case , this animation is clipping and really noticeable.</p>\n<p>However,this is an emote animation, it rarely happened in-game ( unless the player trigger it ), the issue also can be seen in his base skin, and also due to low contrast on clipping so this clipping issue is acceptable and we leave it without address any solution to fix it.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b7f1e3f145657f2e26d4.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b7f1e3f145657f2e26d4.webp\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:500px\" alt=\"Illustration 35\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></div>\n\n<p><strong>Milestone 3 - 4</strong><strong><br></strong></p>\n\n<p>Once everything is done, replay the champion may help us to find some issue that we may not be aware of. However, usually at this point all issue should be really small issues since most of major issues are being covered previously, but this could help minimize Jira tickets later.</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: VFX Render over structure</strong></p><p>One common issue that can be found in VFX is that the effect is in consistently between skin, and we can spot them out and fix it before the skin move to testing phase</p>\n<p>Here is an example of an VFX render over structures issue from Black Frost Reksai compare to her base skinYour browser does not support the HTML5 video element<br><br>Your browser does not support the HTML5 video element</p></div>\n\n<h4>Perforce version control</h4>\n\n<p>In the game, every artist have to access to client's perforce server, so it's important to make sure that every artists must follow the work-flow. Follow up Perforce regularly will also help engineer team on client's side have visibility about their recent update on their tools and game engine.</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>CID</strong></p><p>One of the version control application web-based tools from client is CID, it listed all the update form user via P4 that using a custom submit tool from client. This can help to make sure that all the file packages been updated won't cause any error into the game built</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/996367dd6a9ca7daf9a3.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/996367dd6a9ca7daf9a3.webp\" width=\"1039\" height=\"621\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 36\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>The CID table, noticed that the red box means the change list can cause the game built failed so a person who cause an issue have to solve it</em></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Perforce version control</strong></p><p>Also checking via CID only shown user that follow the work-flow. It's better to also double check on Perforce itself to see if there is anyone submit without using the tools and didn't follow the workflow properly</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d877b10fd4f5aba98c2b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d877b10fd4f5aba98c2b.webp\" width=\"1146\" height=\"823\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 37\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>A Perforce history check to make sure everyone follow the pipeline , noticed that this change list's description isn't programming generated which mean the artist isn't follow the workflow.</em></p></div>\n\n<h4>Daily troubleshooting</h4>\n\n<p>By the time passes, there will be new issue raised by artists during the day, it may block the artist by the day if we don't support them.</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Maya Tools troubleshooting</strong></p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/10dc02cf2b0087aa19ed.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/10dc02cf2b0087aa19ed.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"451\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 38\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><em>Tools issue on Maya</em></p>\n<p>Usually client's will update new feature on their tools, so new issues may happened on the new update. A TA have to look for those issue, fix it if possible and notify clients about the daily issue.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Game Engine troubleshooting</strong></p><p>Similar to Tools, Game Engine sometimes have issue cause by new update or a improperly update from artist's machine . So TA have to make sure they are resolved asap to make sure they didn't get into trouble later.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/19e61151209c3e237af2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/19e61151209c3e237af2.webp\" width=\"960\" height=\"213\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 39\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>An issue caused by improperly update ( it's only happened on one artist's machine )</em></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/2d7b25e9c2bef7750376.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/2d7b25e9c2bef7750376.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"626\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 40\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>The issue caused the game failed to start</em></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Art issue troubleshooting</strong></p><p>Art issue is an issue caused during production due to the limitation between game and maya file that caused the results are difference from original work. The issue sometimes listed on client's feedback, or been noticed by artists and they don't have a solution for it. In this case, TA will investigate an issue and provide a solution for artists so that it can help the production meet the required art quality</p>\n\n<p><em>An animation issue caused when export animation from Maya to Game Engine (example image from documents )</em></p></div>\n\n<h4>Cohesive team member</h4>\n\n<p>Sometime, a technical problem from one discipline could be solved by another discipline. For Example</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Dragon Slayer Diana</strong></p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/86b2c1d006717d2171ec.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/86b2c1d006717d2171ec.webp\" width=\"630\" height=\"636\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 42\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>Glow effect on Diana's chest</em></p>\n<p>The glow effect on Diana's chest VFX isn't shown on her base skin, it's some new VFX that's added only for this skin. Due to that, there is no Joint pivot in that position for VFX artist to add in. So if VFX artist are trying to solve the issue by themselves, they might spend so much time to offset the VFX to the position while this can be done better than just add a new pivot there.</p></div>\n\n<h4>Managing Jira ticket</h4>\n\n<p>After the production is finished, there will be a QA test run to make sure that there is no concern on art/ technical issue on our final product. Any found issue will be submitted as a Jira's ticket and send back to us. The team have to fix the issue until the skin is releases. However, fixing an issue may cause artists overlapped with their recent work, and an issue sometime can be skipped. So the TA will have to manage those tickets and give the ticket to the right person so that won't cause a lot of back and forth. The ticket sometime can be closed without fixing it, so giving a right call is needed to address those issues, this can help reduce the team workload on spending so much time to solve a really tiny issue.</p>\n\n<p>&lt;example won't fix cases due to acceptable &gt;</p>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Issue that is won't fix</strong></p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d3aa5b56da591e574a72.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d3aa5b56da591e574a72.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"701\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 43\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>A Closed as won't fix ticket</em></p>\n<p>The Ticket above is an issue that's been closed without any fix are needed. The reason is the issue are:</p>\n<ul><li>The issue is a minor issue</li><li>The are really low chance that the issue can be triggered</li><li>The effective on the fix is not high ( the player may not notice an issue anyway )</li><li>The scope to fix this issue is high</li></ul>\n<p>=&gt; Not worth the bandwidth to fix an issue.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>Example: Major issue</strong></p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c1d16355ed7d392d5223.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c1d16355ed7d392d5223.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"796\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 44\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><em>A Major issue</em></p>\n<p><em><br></em>The following issue is a high priority and an major issue because:</p>\n<ul><li>There is a high chance to make an issue happen (the player use the skill)</li><li>The issue can affect game play, and the play will notice it.</li></ul>\n<p>=&gt; Action is needed and it has to be done before release to PBE</p></div>\n\n<h4>Enhance team with technical knowledge.</h4>\n\n<p>After working on a several production , artist will certainly increase their art skill. However, enhance their technical knowledge and sharing experience on how to solve a common issue will help them have a proper workflow and be able to unblock themselves when TA is unable to support them.</p>\n\n<h4>More Tools!</h4>\n\n<p>Time passed by, we may found out some bottle neck of the project, where artist keep doing the same task over and over again, in the same pattern. This is where tools are become handy and make their work less painful. Creating a new tools that can enhance those bottle-neck is also one of the responsibility for TA on this project. A bit knowledge of programming for at least have a good library of tools will be great for TA to make some \"black magic\" for the workflow to be better, faster while keeping the high quality of the production.</p>\n\n<p>Case study</p>\n\n<h4><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span>#Case1: Transfer Perforce replica server</h4>\n\n<p>In Sep 2019, clients have notified us that they will change P4 server to a new branch to increase tools and Perforce server latency. At the same time, the internal team were ramping up from 2 pods to 4, so there were a training were happened for a artists.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Issue</strong></p>\n\n<ul><li>Client want to transfer everyone to a new server ASAP.</li><li>The production are undergoing and all artists work have to move over new server as well.</li><li>Training are on going and new artist are using old server to training as well, so it's not a good idea to move them to a new server.</li></ul>\n\n<p><strong>Solutions</strong></p>\n\n<ul><li>We reach out to client about the training is happening so request to remain the old server until training is done, therefore this won't cause so much time setup for trainee. At the same time we schedule with internal team when the transfer will be happened and remind artists to submit everything until the end of the day. By taking the advantage of time differences with client, the transfer happened on client's Friday, which is our Saturday morning, so that all data could be able to transfer over without left any work behind.</li><li>Once client notified that everything is transferred to the new server, we move all production team to it on Monday, while the trainee remain on the old server.</li><li>The server transfer taken only a morning, and since everything was tested before hand ( as TA already test on the new server previously to ensure that artist are able to work on the new server). One the training side, once the training is done, we move the rest of trainee to the new server and notified client that we are good to go now.</li><li>time</li><li><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b69db51dc821883671ff.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b69db51dc821883671ff.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"350\" style=\"--source-width:542px\" alt=\"Illustration 45\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></li><li><em>Timeline of the transferring server process</em></li><li><strong>Results</strong></li><li>We still got a blocker for 2 days after the transfer is done, due to hurricane on Japan caused the connection to the P4 server down.... The project... However the transfer was successfully and smooth enough that doesn't take more than a day to setup for artists.</li></ul>\n\n<h4>#Case2: QC Tools integration into client's game engine.</h4>\n\n<p>In Sep 2020, internal discussion have been raised by VFX artists about the number of QC check-list that's need to be done in optimization phases. These, in results, are the cause that sometimes artist might missed some of the check-list because of a number of work that's they've been done over the pass month for a skin ( each skin has at least 20 up to 50 VFXs depend on a champion, each VFXs can have up to 10 emitters on it, which is a lot of things to check! )</p>\n\n<p><strong>Issue</strong></p>\n\n<ul><li>There isn't any tools to make such a QC for this in RE before</li><li>An artists may take up to a day just to finish this tasks and may still missed out some emitter.</li></ul>\n\n<p><strong>The Tool</strong></p>\n\n<p>After gathering feedbacks from artists, we have broken down into some key QC check and some core feature that we need to have for a tool that can be useful.</p>\n\n<ul><li>The must have:</li></ul>\n\n<ul><li>Tools must be-able to work with the recent features that is needed and can be extendable in the future if more requests are coming</li><li>The QC must be-able to check for most-cased and situation.</li></ul>\n\n<ul><li>The should have:</li></ul>\n\n<ul><li>After it's been done internally, which mean the core feature is working, it's better to share the knowledge to client and see if we could intergrade it into their engine</li></ul>\n\n<p><strong>Tool's QC features (WIP, more is coming)</strong></p>\n\n<ul><li>Check for disabled emitter</li><li>Check if the emitters have disabled Zbuffer option (additional feature is to white-list any emitter that's needed to disable Zbuffer )</li><li>Check for duplicated textures images</li><li>Check if the textures that they were using is stored in the correct folder ( or using the correct image's layer )</li></ul>\n\n<p>After reading through some sample json file, we found out some good data to create a sample tools and make an internal tools up for testing.Your browser does not support the HTML5 video element</p>\n\n<p><em>The core features of the QC tools</em></p>\n\n<p>For now, the tool has been propose to client and they are really like the concept of it. It's now starting to re-work on the tools by using GDS's API, the API that's using for RE, and will be a part of the tools in RE in the futures and will be used for both outsourcer as well as Riot's internal.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/fad95a32489a06ba4a16.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/fad95a32489a06ba4a16.webp\" width=\"890\" height=\"723\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 46\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>New scripting that's now using Riot pipeline API.</p>";
